§ `Regulation 37`

#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `attendance allowance in accordance with section 64 of the 1992 Act`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `pension age disability payment in accordance with the Disability Assistance for Older People (Scotland) Regulations 2024`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the care component of disability living allowance in accordance with section 72 of the 1992 Act, at the middle or highest rate`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `an increase in the rate of disablement pension in accordance with section 104 of the 1992 Act`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `a benefit payable as if the injury or disease were one for which a disablement pension would be payable on an assessment of 100 per cent., by virtue of the Pneumoconiosis, Byssinosis and Miscellaneous Diseases Benefit Scheme 1983 or regulations made under section 64(3) of the 2012 Act`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `a constant attendance allowance payable by virtue of article 8 of the Naval, Military and Air Forces etc. (Disablement and Death) Service Pensions Order 2006 or article 14 of the Personal Injuries (Civilians) Scheme 1983`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the daily living component of personal independence payment in accordance with section 78 of the 2012 Act`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `armed forces independence payment in accordance with the Armed Forces and Reserve Forces (Compensation Scheme) Order 2011`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the care component of child disability payment at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 11 of the Disability Assistance for Children and Young People (Scotland) Regulations 2021`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate in accordance with regulation 5 of the Disability Assistance for Working Age People (Scotland) Regulations 2022`
#ASSERT `regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `the care component of Scottish adult disability living allowance at the middle or highest rate in accordance with regulation 6(4) of the Disability Assistance (Scottish Adult Disability Living Allowance) Regulations 2025`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 37(4): the benefit is a relevant benefit` `no benefit that regulation 37(4) lists`)

