#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received on the last day of the following tax year`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received a day later`)
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received within the first following year`
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received late with a further time allowed to 31 Dec 2027`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received after a further time allowed to 31 Dec 2027`)
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week in 2025, received in time though a further time of 1 Jan 2027 was allowed`
-- The week is counted in the tax year in which it begins (regulation 25(3)).
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week starting 5 Apr 2026 (tax year 2025), received on 5 Apr 2027`
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week starting 6 Apr 2026 (tax year 2026), received on 5 Apr 2027`
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week starting 6 Apr 2026 (tax year 2026), received on 5 Apr 2028`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 39: the application is received in time` `week starting 6 Apr 2026 (tax year 2026), received on 6 Apr 2028`)
-- (b): as written, a regulation 35 application must be received AFTER the end of the year of the week; no latest date (fork F31).
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 39: the application is received in time` `regulation 35 application, week in 2025, received on the last day of that tax year`)
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `regulation 35 application, week in 2025, received the day after that tax year ends`
#ASSERT NOT (`regulation 39: the application is received in time` `regulation 35 application, week in 2025, received during that tax year`)
#ASSERT `regulation 39: the application is received in time` `regulation 35 application, week in 2025, received in 2040`
